/target
# Any standalone workspace (a spike, a fuzz target) has its own target
# directory that the root-anchored rule above does not cover.
**/target/
**/*.rs.bk
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.log
/recovery
/history
/clipboard
/index
/embeddings
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
!.vscode/settings.json
# Per-run local CI records. Benchmark results under artifacts/benchmarks/ are
# deliberately NOT ignored -- they are the evidence behind ADR-0015.
artifacts/test-evidence/*.json

# Built release archives and their checksums. The *script* that produces them
# is the artefact worth keeping (scripts/New-Release.ps1); a 21 MB zip
# reproducible from one commit is not, and a repository that carries its own
# binaries is one nobody can clone quickly.
artifacts/releases/*.zip
artifacts/releases/*.tar.gz
artifacts/releases/SHA256SUMS.txt

# Documents saved into the checkout by accident. Save As used to default to
# the process working directory, so testing the app from this directory wrote
# real notes straight into the repo -- and one commit later they were pushed.
# The dialogs now default to the document's folder or Documents; this is the
# second line of defence. Root level only, so docs/ and notes/ are unaffected.
/*.txt
/*.md
!/README.md
!/CLAUDE.md
!/DECISIONS.md
!/PROJECT_MEMORY.md
!/ROADMAP.md
!/specs.md
# The three a public repository needs, added 2026-09-10 -- and every one of
# them was written, staged and *silently dropped* by the rule above before
# anybody checked. `git status` does not list an ignored file, so the failure
# is invisible in exactly the place somebody would look for it.
#
# The general form, which is why this comment is longer than the lines: a
# deny-by-default rule with an allowlist is safe and **its failure mode is
# silence**. Any new file at the root has to be added here or it does not
# exist as far as the repository is concerned.
!/CONTRIBUTING.md
!/SECURITY.md
!/THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md

# Agent worktrees. A subagent working in isolation gets a git worktree here,
# which is a repository inside this one -- `git add -A` sweeps it into a
# commit as a stray gitlink if it is not ignored. It happened once.
/.claude/worktrees/

# A personal `.code-workspace` at the root -- how somebody opens this repo,
# not part of it. `.vscode/settings.json` above is the shared half and stays
# tracked; this is the half that differs per person, and an untracked file at
# the root also blocks `New-Release.ps1`, which refuses to build a release
# from a tree nobody can check out again.
/*.code-workspace

# Playwright MCP scratch output -- screenshots and page snapshots taken while
# checking the site renders. Evidence for one session, not part of the repo.
/.playwright-mcp/

# The signup function's dependencies. Azure Static Web Apps installs them at
# deploy time from api/package.json; a committed node_modules would be tens of
# megabytes of somebody else's code in a repository whose whole licence story
# is about knowing exactly what it ships.
/site/api/node_modules/

# The manual, staged into the site by .github/workflows/site.yml at deploy
# time. `docs/generated/manual.html` is the committed copy with a staleness
# check over it; a second one here would be a third home for the same bytes
# and the one nothing checks.
/site/docs/
